injures his right leg. Accompanied by his
parents, he is now in the Emergency
Department. He has a 5 mm deep laceration in
a 2x3 abrasion on his right leg. The wound is
contaminated with soil. You disinfect the wound
and ask his parents about his tetanus
vaccination status. He has received 2 doses of
DTPa at 2 and 4 months of age, but not the
third dose at 6 months or thereafter. Which one
of the following is the appropriate management
