visit a 65-year-old inward patient for
agitation. When you arrive at the ward, you
are informed that she underwent
cholecystectomy 48 hours ago. Her file shows
that she received prophylactic amoxicillin
before the surgery. On examination, she is
confused and delirious and has a blood
pressure of 135/87 mmHg, heart rate of 110,
and temperature of 38.4°C. She is agitated
and difficult to deal with. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate next step in
