emergency department after he collapsed
while surfing. On examination, he is tanned,
has a blood pressure of 80/60 mmHg, and a
pulse rate of 100 bpm. You draw blood and
Start him on intravenous fluids. A bolus of
500 ml of normal saline is given, and since
there is no response, you give him another 2
liters of normal saline in 2 hours; however,
his blood pressure remains low. His
laboratory results are back and are
remarkable for a serum sodium level of 124
mmol/L and potassium of 6 mmol/L (3.5-5.5).
