on risedronate 35mg weekly after she was
diagnosed with osteoporosis, confirmed with
bone mineral density (BMD). Her presenting
symptom at that time was back pain.
Examination revealed a height decrease, mild
kyphosis, and tenderness over thoracic
vertebrae. Despite being on risedronate, her
symptoms persisted, and she also developed
pain over new areas of her thoracic vertebrae. A
new X-ray established new osteoporotic
fractures. Which of the following would be the
most appropriate management option for her?','{"A":"Continue residronate at the same\ndose.","B":"Switch to alendronate.","C":"Increase the dose of residronate.","D":"Switch to zoledronic acid.","E":"Switch to teriparatide."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-0cc3c4d08d8a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"c90945caca0ea9affc40","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_page":201,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"c90945caca0ea9affc40","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":201,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Endocrine/Breast","stem":"Three months ago, you started Mary, aged 73,\non risedronate 35mg weekly after she was\ndiagnosed with osteoporosis, confirmed with\nbone mineral density (BMD). Her presenting\nsymptom at that time was back pain.\nExamination revealed a height decrease, mild\nkyphosis, and tenderness over thoracic\nvertebrae. Despite being on risedronate, her\nsymptoms persisted, and she also developed\npain over new areas of her thoracic vertebrae. A\nnew X-ray established new osteoporotic\nfractures. Which of the following would be the\nmost appropriate management option for her?","options":{"A":"Continue residronate at the same\ndose.","B":"Switch to alendronate.","C":"Increase the dose of residronate.","D":"Switch to zoledronic acid.","E":"Switch to teriparatide."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_im