with a swelling in the left lower part of her neck.
The swelling has developed over the past four
months, is painless, and feels rubbery and
regular on palpation with no tenderness. She is
otherwise healthy and asymptomatic.
Ultrasound confirms the presence of a thyroid
nodule; therefore, you perform a fine needle
aspiration (FNA) sampling and send it for
pathology assessment. The pathology
result reports only the presence of follicular
cells. Which of the following would be the most
appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"CT scan of the neck.","B":"Direct laryngoscopy.","C":"MRI of the neck.","D":"Repeat the FNA.","E":"Excisional biopsy of the lump."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","supporting_pages":[226],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-3b9e1a5da45f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e71485570bda9be19394","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_page":226,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"e71485570bda9be19394","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Endo_ breast 1-50.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":226,"supporting_pages":[226],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Endocrine/Breast","stem":"A 55-year-old woman presents to your clinic\nwith a swelling in the left lower part of her neck.\nThe swelling has developed over the past four\nmonths, is painless, and feels rubbery and\nregular on palpation with no tenderness. She is\notherwise healthy and asymptomatic.\nUltrasound confirms the presence of a thyroid\nnodule; therefore, you perform a fine needle\naspiration (FNA) sampling and send it for\npathology assessment. The pathology\nresult reports only the presence of follicular\ncells. Which of the following would be the most\nappropriate next step in management?","options":{"A":"CT scan of the neck.","B":"Direct laryngoscopy.","C":"MRI of the neck.","D":"Repeat the FNA.","E":"Excisional biopsy of the lump."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer