has come to your office today for a health
check. During the session, you notice that she
is sad and worried, and is vaguely trying to
communicate her concerns. Further probing
reveals the issue. Her 16-year-old son is an
addict and a drug dealer. She has been
frequently beaten by him when she refuses to
give him money for drugs. Which one of the
following is the most important next step to
consider regarding her problem?','{"A":"Call the police.","B":"Tell her to seek shelter in a women’s\nrefuge center.","C":"Inform the child protection service.","D":"Admit the son to a rehabilitation\ncenter.","E":"Arrange an appointment with the son."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 1.pdf","supporting_pages":[1],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-94a3f4a3ac7f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"3cad5e109056aecf5515","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 1.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 1.pdf","source_page":1,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"3cad5e109056aecf5515","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 1.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 1.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":1,"supporting_pages":[1],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Ethics/Population Health","stem":"Martha, 54 years old, is a patient of yours, who\nhas come to your office today for a health\ncheck. During the session, you notice that she\nis sad and worried, and is vaguely trying to\ncommunicate her concerns. Further probing\nreveals the issue. Her 16-year-old son is an\naddict and a drug dealer. She has been\nfrequently beaten by him when she refuses to\ngive him money for drugs. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most important next step to\nconsider regarding her problem?","options":{"A":"Call the police.","B":"Tell her to seek shelter in a women’s\nrefuge center.","C":"Inform the child protection service.","D":"Admit the son to a rehabilitation\ncenter.","E":"Arrange an appointment with the son."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_imp